# Project intentions

Read [docs/INTENTIONS.md](docs/INTENTIONS.md) before expanding scope.

## Stay in v1/v2/v3/v4/v5/v6/v7/v8

Allowed: app + Go `/forecast` resource, nested overlay panel, prediction interval bands, `showInterval`, training window independent of the panel time range (from/to picker), forecast window (Auto `now` → `now` + model duration) with a reason when empty, type-keyed train-query adapters (Prometheus range, OpenSearch metric+histogram or PPL time series, Postgres time-series SQL) and labeled/wide-frame extract/match, Postgres snapshot store (pgx) and skip-train until Retrain, mergeable `grafana.ini` `[plugin.eduardkolotushin-forecast-app]` and `[plugin.eduardkolotushin-forecast-datasource]` snippet for CI/CD, nested forecast datasource (`QueryData` Restore) so Grafana alerting can use forecast / interval by `refId`.

Do **not** add without updating INTENTIONS first:

- Docker Compose / TestData sandbox (sibling `timeseries-grafana-sandbox`)
- Kubernetes Helm / images (sibling `timeseries-k8s`)
- Grafana.com signing/publish
- Prometheus, OpenSearch, or Postgres **datasource HTTP** in `pkg/`
- Elasticsearch plugin type
- Shipping Grafana alert rules or contact points
- A forked Series or forecast implementation
- Extra app pages beyond landing + Configuration
- A Druid/Kafka ticker in this plugin (sibling `timeseries-baselines`)

## Use the sibling libraries

Call `timeseries` and `timeseries-forecast` through their public APIs. Depend on tagged module versions; do not add a `replace` directive.
